Z||000000||DrRodey||04-09-2001||11:30 AM||||Problem time in Rodey-ville... <P>I just completely lost the suspension on my Jeep.  (damn Pot holes)  So I need to get a fiero runnin Quick.. <P>I have two days, Friday and Sat.  and three choices<P>1:  Resplice the main cable of the wiring harness comin out of the computer since a damn mouse chewed through it sometime over the winter.(85)<P>2:  Completely replace the wireing harness. (85)<P>3:  Swap the engines between my 85 and T-top to get the t-top runnin again. (note, these two cars are currently 25 miles apart.)  Planning an Engine swap (g2 sc 3800) anyway so do i want to swap another 4banger in first???<P>Right now i'm voting for #1 based on time and ease.  <BR>Any other options are welcome as well.  This will be my main car for some time.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>Hi... My names Dan, and i'm addicted to Fieros.<BR>'88 Formula CONVERTIBLE<BR>'85 Coupe<BR>'84 coupe T-Top<BR>AOL IM = drrodey<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.JPG">   <BR> <A HREF="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html" TARGET=_blank>freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html</A>||||reg||5
